---
// Why Stilton cannot be made in Stilton, nor, the old way, called it.
---

<p>
	Stilton has never been made in Stilton.
</p>
<p>
	When the cheese got its protected name in 1996, the line was drawn round the three counties where it was made: Derbyshire, Leicestershire and
	Nottinghamshire. Stilton is in Cambridgeshire, so a cheese made in Stilton cannot be called Stilton.
</p>
<p class="milk-story-source">
	Sources: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stilton_cheese" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikipedia, Stilton cheese</a>
</p>
